# MathEducation

Work only on abstract mathematics, its sources, typed relations and derived UI. Never import student records, academy accounts, passwords, sessions or source code from another repository.

Read docs/CONTEXT_MANIFEST.json, provenance/export-coverage.json and docs/ACCESS_HANDOFF.json first. Load only the selected concept/relation/evidence and matching contracts. Current contracts are canonical Schema 1.3.0, registry 1.3.0 and authoring 1.1.0; older source attachments are preserved history.

The four full domain JSON workpacks and curriculum-boundary.json are missing. Do not reconstruct or promote UI projections into canonical inputs. A full relation audit remains blocked: 143 of 918 assertions were individually read; 775 were not. Imported originals need exact binding/hash verification before audit coverage changes.

Preserve stable concept, term-sense, notation-context and relation IDs. Atomic concepts, classification parents, mathematical requirements, representation and teaching perspective are different contracts. Official source edition/location supports curriculum scope; AI/model explanations and translations have separate provenance. Keep official grade bands distinct from unverified year placement.

selected is not approved. Existing Actions marked contract_only are design contracts, not enabled execution tools. Screen position, zoom, selection and filters are derived view state. A changed source hash invalidates affected formula/translation annotations, views and caches.

Do not retry or route around the blocked Correspondence Page notice write. Respect every prior access/approval denial; a fresh cloud environment does not remove it. Space access in a future Cloud task is unverified. Work from this export when those tools are unavailable.

Before finishing run bun run validate. A passing digest/test check establishes supplied bytes and code behavior; it is not an exhaustive mathematical, teacher, accessibility or Cloud runtime review. Use docs/CODEX_CLOUD.md for setup and docs/KICKOFF.md for the next bounded task.
